---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FlowHero from '../../components/FlowHero.astro';
import OldFlow from '../../components/OldFlow.astro';
import { site, projects } from '../../data/site';
import Check from '@lucide/astro/icons/check';

const project = projects.find((p) => p.slug === 'evertune')!;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title={`${project.title} · ${site.name}`} description={project.summary}>
	<article class="container study">
		<a class="back" href={`${base}/#work`}>← All case studies</a>

		<ul class="tags">
			{project.tags.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}
		</ul>
		<h1>{project.title}</h1>

		<section>
			<h2>Overview</h2>
			<p>
				Evertune customers have more than one way to create the prompts that measure their AI visibility.
				They can start from a standard template, or use Evertune’s agent to create prompts based on how
				people actually prompt LLMs.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Context</h2>
			<p>
				At first, there was only one way to create prompts: the standard template. As Evertune grew and we
				gathered more feedback, we learned that customers wanted to run their own sets of prompts, so we added
				a new type of analysis.
			</p>
			<p>
				Before we knew it, there were five different ways to create prompts. Each was added to meet a specific
				customer need, but over time the whole thing became unwieldy and hard to use.
			</p>
			<p>
				Very soon, we started hearing from new users that the prompt creation flow took too much time and was
				hard to use.
			</p>
			<div class="growth" aria-label="From one way to create prompts to five">
				<div>
					<span class="count">1</span>
					<span class="what">way to create prompts</span>
				</div>
				<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
				<div>
					<span class="count">5</span>
					<span class="what">ways, each added for a specific customer need</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>The problem</h2>
			<p>
				Getting to a set of prompts took many steps, and customers, especially new users, struggled to pick the
				right type of tracker. There were five main types, and one of them had three steps of its own. It was
				confusing before anyone had written a single prompt.
			</p>
			<OldFlow />
			<p class="figcap">How tracker creation worked before. The path shown is Suggested prompts.</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>The insight</h2>
			<p>
				After collecting user feedback and analyzing how customers use the platform, it became clear that one
				primary flow served 80% of users.
			</p>
			<div class="growth" aria-label="80% of users are served by one primary flow">
				<div>
					<span class="count">80%</span>
					<span class="what">of users were served by one primary flow</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Design direction</h2>
			<p>
				I also wanted the design to align with Evertune’s long-term vision of an agentic platform experience.
				After learning more about the tools our customers already used, a chat-to-canvas flow felt like a
				natural fit.
			</p>
			<div class="growth" aria-label="Chat to canvas">
				<div>
					<span class="count">Chat</span>
				</div>
				<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
				<div>
					<span class="count">Canvas</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>The new experience</h2>
			<p>
				With the new agent experience, there is nothing to choose up front. Users begin prompt creation
				in a simple chat, use Evertune’s agent to modify the topics and prompts, and adjust the settings
				before running.
			</p>
			<FlowHero steps={project.flow!} />
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>The impact</h2>
			<p class="pull">
				New customers find it much easier and more intuitive to create trackers and run prompts.
			</p>
			<ul class="wins">
				<li><Check size={20} strokeWidth={1.75} aria-hidden="true" />No onboarding steps needed</li>
				<li>
					<Check size={20} strokeWidth={1.75} aria-hidden="true" />No white-glove service from our customer success team
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
	.study {
		max-width: 900px;
		padding-top: 140px;
		padding-bottom: 40px;
	}
	.back {
		display: inline-block;
		color: var(--muted);
		text-decoration: none;
		margin-bottom: 28px;
	}
	.back:hover {
		color: var(--accent);
	}
	h1 {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-weight: 400;
		font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
		line-height: 1.1;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		margin: 16px 0 12px;
	}
	section {
		margin-top: 56px;
	}
	section p {
		max-width: 62ch;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		color: var(--fg);
	}
	.tags {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 0;
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 8px;
	}
	.tags li {
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		color: var(--muted);
		border: 1px solid rgba(90, 50, 30, 0.12);
		border-radius: 999px;
		padding: 2px 10px;
	}
	.growth {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 12px 32px;
		margin-top: 32px;
		padding: 24px 28px;
		border-radius: 16px;
		background: linear-gradient(121deg, #ffffff 0%, #fff3ec 100%);
		border: 1px solid rgba(90, 50, 30, 0.07);
	}
	.growth > div {
		display: flex;
		align-items: baseline;
		gap: 14px;
	}
	.count {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: 3.4rem;
		line-height: 1;
		font-variant-numeric: lining-nums;
		color: #b0694a;
	}
	.what {
		color: var(--muted);
		max-width: 18ch;
		line-height: 1.35;
	}
	.arrow {
		font-size: 1.6rem;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.arrow {
			display: none;
		}
	}
	section p.pull {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.4vw, 2.3rem);
		line-height: 1.25;
		max-width: 28ch;
		margin: 0 0 24px;
	}
	.wins {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: 12px;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
	}
	.wins li {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 12px;
	}
	.wins :global(svg) {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		padding: 5px;
		box-sizing: content-box;
		width: 20px;
		height: 20px;
		border-radius: 8px;
		background: #fbede5;
		color: #b0694a;
	}
	section p.figcap {
		margin: 12px auto 0;
		text-align: center;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}
</style>
